  "query_preview": "..A weather system moving through the Great Basin \nover the next 24 hours has brought breezy to windy conditions \ntoday to southeast Arizona and then a little less wind on \nMonday. See fire weather section below for additional details \non the elevated to near critical fire weather conditions through\nMonday.\n\nBaggy trofiness will remain over the desert southwest for the\nremainder of the work week into the weekend. There are hints in\nthe ensemble/deterministic models of a weak influx of mid-level\nmoisture into the eastern zones that may result in some build-\nups or a very low end 10-15% chance of high-based mainly dry \nthunderstorms next weekend over the eastern mountains.\n\nBelow normal high temperatures today and Monday before warming \nup to near normal by Wednesday and remaining in this area into \nnext weekend.\n\n8-14 day outlook (May 25-31):\nTemperature: Leaning above normal (33-45%) \nPrecipitation: Likely above normal (50-60%)",
